    - BOTH RMSNorms of every offloaded layer (--ops does not include 'norm': its C-1 re-entry is the B-FEED-WIDTH cost)
    - the SwiGLU product of every offloaded layer (--ops does not include 'swiglu', same reason)
    - the RoPE of the CACHED K rows: the rotated K must reach the KVQ codec as exact fp16 bits and the tile's q_sink egress is a C-1 view (B-ROPE-EGRESS) — decode-token q rows only
